    "title": "League City leaders crack down on public camping, panhandling after increase in homeless encampments - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Julianna Washburn, Galveston County Bureau ,\n7 hours ago The city now requires written permission to camp on private property and puts limits on what is allowed in public spaces, such as abandoned or unattended personal property. The League City Council approved updates to existing city ordinances Tuesday night to crack down on public camping and panhandling around the city. Read full article",
